  "text": "Oncology For Dogs & Cats | Veterinary Oncologist Specialists\nSkip to content\n03 9050 0671\nMon-Fri: 8am to 6pm\nSat-Sun: Emergency specialist referral surgery only\nHome\nServices\nHospital Services\nSurgery\nNeurosurgery\nDiagnostic Imaging\nInternal Medicine\nOncology\nMobile Services\nMobile Orthopaedic Surgery\nMobile Soft Tissue Surgery\nOncology Telehealth Consults\nReferring Vets\nRefer Online\nNew Vet Registration\nReferring Vet Login\nPet Owners\nAbout\nMeet the Team\nLatest News\nFAQs\nContact\nHome\nServices\nHospital Services\nSurgery\nNeurosurgery\nDiagnostic Imaging\nInternal Medicine\nOncology\nMobile Services\nMobile Orthopaedic Surgery\nMobile Soft Tissue Surgery\nOncology Telehealth Consults\nReferring Vets\nRefer Online\nNew Vet Registration\nReferring Vet Login\nPet Owners\nAbout\nMeet the Team\nLatest News\nFAQs\nContact\nHome\nServices\nHospital Services\nSurgery\nNeurosurgery\nDiagnostic Imaging\nInternal Medicine\nOncology\nMobile Services\nMobile Orthopaedic Surgery\nMobile Soft Tissue Surgery\nOncology Telehealth Consults\nReferring Vets\nRefer Online\nNew Vet Registration\nReferring Vet Login\nPet Owners\nAbout\nMeet the Team\nLatest News\nFAQs\nContact\nHome\nServices\nHospital Services\nSurgery\nNeurosurgery\nDiagnostic Imaging\nInternal Medicine\nOncology\nMobile Services\nMobile Orthopaedic Surgery\nMobile Soft Tissue Surgery\nOncology Telehealth Consults\nReferring Vets\nRefer Online\nNew Vet Registration\nReferring Vet Login\nPet Owners\nAbout\nMeet the Team\nLatest News\nFAQs\nContact\nOncology For Dogs & Cats\nOncology for dogs and cats is at the heart of what we do at MARS, engaging all services within every cancer treatment plan.\nOur Veterinary Oncology Specialists Are Leading the Way\nWith cancer affecting 1 in 4 dogs and up to 1 in 3 cats, our veterinary oncology specialists provide a comprehensive range of treatment options, including surgery, medical therapies, and interventional oncology. Our commitment to understanding cancer in pets not only enhances treatment outcomes but also contributes to broader advancements in cancer care across all species, ensuring the best possible support for our patients and their families. In order to work as efficiently as possible clients will usually meet our oncology vet team first to discuss all available options and to then tailor diagnostic and treatment needs from there.\nComprehensive Vet Cancer Care\nVeterinary Oncology\nMARS offers comprehensive cancer care for pets, combining advanced diagnostics, personalised treatment plans, and compassionate support to ensure the best possible outcomes for dogs and cats facing cancer.\nRead more\nOncology Surgery\nSurgical intervention is often the most effective treatment for solid tumours.\nMARS’s expert surgical team utilises advanced techniques, including Near-Infrared Fluorescence (NIRF) Lymphatic Imaging, to enhance tumour removal and improve recovery times.\nRead more\nCancer Diagnostics\nAccurate diagnosis is crucial in oncology for cats and dogs and the following treatment.\nMARS employs state-of-the-art diagnostic tools to identify cancer types and stages, enabling the development of targeted and effective treatment plans.\nRead more\nOncology Treatments\nBeyond conventional therapies, MARS provides cutting-edge medical treatments tailored to each pet’s specific cancer type, whether canine cancer treatment or feline lung cancer treatment is required or  aiming to maximise efficacy while minimising side effects.\nRead more\nChemotherapy\nMARS offers chemotherapy protocols designed to treat various cancers in pets, focusing on maintaining quality of life and managing side effects through individualised treatment plans. If you need to find out the cat or dog chemotherapy cost give our oncology vet team a call today.\nRead more\nTargeted Cancer Therapy\nUtilising therapies that specifically target cancer cells, MARS aims to reduce harm to healthy tissues, offering treatments that are both effective and have fewer side effects compared to traditional methods. Our oncology for cats and dogs\nRead more\nImmunotherapy\nMARS provides immunotherapy options that stimulate a pet’s immune system to recognise and combat cancer cells, offering a personalised approach to cancer treatment.\nRead more\nElectrochemotherapy\nThis treatment combines chemotherapy with electrical pulses to enhance drug uptake by cancer cells, particularly effective for treating skin and subcutaneous tumours in pets.\n​\nRead more\nPalliative Care\nFocused on comfort and quality of life, MARS’s palliative care services address pain management and symptom relief for pets with serious illnesses, supporting both pets and their families throughout the treatment journey.\nRead more\nRefer Online Today\nOur wonderful team are ready to provide the best care\nMake a referral\nWe are dedicated to achieving the best possible outcomes for every pet and pet owner.\nWe accept\nVetPay\nand\nAfterpay.\nVisit our sister hospital for more specialist support at Geelong Animal Referral Services\nContact us\n03 9050 0671\nenquiries@marsvets.com.au\n619 Whitehorse Road, Mitcham VIC 3132\nMon-Fri: 8am to 6pm\nSat-Sun: Emergency specialist referral surgery only\nFacebook\nInstagram\nLinkedin\n© 2025 Melbourne Animal Referral Services  |\nPrivacy\nABN: 76 652 987 310\nMARS IS MOVING!\nFrom\nMonday,\n31\nst\nAugust\n,\nwe will be located at our NEW address:\n619 Whitehorse Road,\nMitcham VIC 3132.\nPlease contact our team if you have any questions.\nGet in touch\nGet directions\nWE’VE MOVED — FIND US AT 619 WHITEHORSE ROAD, MITCHAM VIC 3132.\nGet directions",
